---
/*
 * /about/ - institutional About page.
 *
 * Source content: editorial/drafts/about_page.md (style-editor pass complete,
 * TK-free, ~340 words). The body is short and well-bounded, so we render the
 * prose inline as HTML rather than route it through Astro's markdown loader
 * (which would add an indirection for a single page with no per-edit churn).
 * The draft remains the source of truth; if it is rewritten, the inline copy
 * here is hand-resynced.
 *
 * Visual register: Vignelli (per design/design-system.md). One sans (Manrope)
 * for everything; H1 in display-lg 800; body in body-lg 400; institutional
 * kicker in micro-caps 600 above the title band. Footer carries the page-end
 * rule; no pillar / section chrome (this is institutional, not editorial).
 *
 * The page is reachable from the footer (VignelliColophon's secondary nav)
 * and NOT from the masthead - the masthead remains the 7 sections + Research.
 */

import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/sections";

const pageTitle = "About";
const pageDesc =
  "Sibley Creek is a standing, opinionated read of the Canadian macro " +
  "picture, organized as a small set of sections that mirror how a Canadian " +
  "institutional desk frames the economy. It exists to help a reader who " +
  "already knows the basics form a sharper view of Canada than the median " +
  "Big-Six economics note.";
---
<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDesc} pageClass="static-page">
  <article class="static" aria-labelledby="static-h">
    <header class="static__header">
      <p class="static__kicker">
        <span class="static__kicker-tok">{site.name}</span>
        <span class="static__kicker-sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <span class="static__kicker-tok static__kicker-tok--name">About</span>
      </p>

      <div class="static__band">
        <h1 id="static-h" class="static__h">About</h1>
      </div>

      <hr class="static__rule" aria-hidden="true" />
    </header>

    <div class="static__body markdown-body">
      <p>
        Sibley Creek is a standing, opinionated read of the Canadian macro
        picture, organized as a small set of sections that mirror how a
        Canadian institutional desk frames the economy and refreshed on
        cadences that match how those sections actually move. It exists to
        help a reader who already knows the basics form a sharper view of
        Canada than the median Big-Six economics note.
      </p>

      <p>
        Canada is the subject. The Fed's path, US growth, Chinese demand, and
        global oil enter only as transmission channels &mdash; into the BoC's
        reaction function, into Canadian export demand, into Canadian
        exporter margins. A piece that could run unchanged in a US shop does
        not belong here.
      </p>

      <p>
        The publication runs across seven sections &mdash; GDP, Inflation,
        Labour, Housing, Policy, Markets, Trade &mdash; each anchored to a
        single headline question. Is the economy at potential, growing, or
        contracting? Is the 2% target being met, on what measures and what
        breadth? How tight is the labour market, and is per-capita output
        recovering? Each section is a chartbook: a vertical stack of
        indicators, each paired with a two-to-four-sentence interpretation
        paragraph. The chart is the evidence; the paragraph is the read.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sibley Creek is tri-modal. A live tracker pulls daily-refresh data
        from primary sources. Short interpretation paragraphs are drafted
        against each fresh print and pass human review before publish.
        Slower, human-led deep dives sit inside the section they belong to,
        dated and contestable. The three modes share one set of sections,
        one voice, one canon.
      </p>

      <p>
        The publication cites Statistics Canada, the Bank of Canada, the
        Department of Finance, the PBO, the provinces, CMHC, OSFI, C.D.
        Howe, the IMF, and the OECD &mdash; not bank morning notes. The
        Big-Six economics desks are competitors to measure against, not
        voices to quote. Constructed series carry a methodology note one
        click away.
      </p>

      <p>
        The name comes from Sibley Creek, a small stream on the Sibley
        Peninsula in Sleeping Giant Provincial Park on the north shore of
        Lake Superior. We took the creek rather than the Giant because
        naming the publication after the landmark would have overclaimed
        &mdash; the creek is the more honest address. The brand mark uses
        the Giant: three flat-topped mesas separated by two erosion
        notches, reclining on his back.
      </p>

      <figure class="static__figure">
        <img
          class="static__figure-img"
          src="/about/sleeping-giant.jpg"
          alt="The Sleeping Giant landform on the Sibley Peninsula in Lake Superior. Three flat-topped diabase mesas separated by erosion notches; the silhouette reads as a reclining figure."
          width="1440"
          height="810"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption class="static__figcaption">
          <span class="static__figcaption-eyebrow">
            The Sleeping Giant, Sibley Peninsula, Lake Superior
          </span>
          <span class="static__figcaption-credit">
            Photo by D.&nbsp;Gordon&nbsp;E.&nbsp;Robertson, CC&nbsp;BY-SA&nbsp;3.0.
          </span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        Sibley Creek is written by Jay Zhao-Murray, formerly Canada
        economics data editor at Bloomberg in Ottawa and, before that, a
        foreign-exchange analyst at Monex Canada covering the loonie. He
        held a research-assistant post at the Bank of Canada and studied
        economics at Western.
      </p>

      <p>
        New data lands when the Canadian release calendar says it does. New
        deep dives ship when there is something to say.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    /* ============================================================
     * /about/ + /methodology/ - shared "static page" surface.
     *
     * Modeled on the /research/<slug>/ deep-dive page, but trimmed:
     *   - No section kicker (this is institutional, not editorial).
     *   - No deck or published-date stamp.
     *   - No "Back to research" foot link.
     * The body markdown-body rules mirror the deep-dive rules so the
     * typographic register matches across the site.
     * ============================================================ */

    .static {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: var(--col-wide);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding-top: 28px;
      padding-bottom: var(--s-9);
    }

    /* ---- Header band ---- */
    .static__kicker {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0 10px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 10px;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .static__kicker-tok { display: inline-block; }
    .static__kicker-tok--name { font-weight: 800; }
    .static__kicker-sep {
      color: var(--ink);
      opacity: 0.32;
      font-weight: 400;
    }

    .static__band {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
      padding-top: 18px;
    }
    .static__h {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 56px);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.018em;
      color: var(--ink);
      max-width: 22ch;
    }

    .static__rule {
      border: 0;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
      margin: 32px 0 0;
    }

    /* ---- Body ---- */
    .static__body {
      margin-top: var(--s-7);
      max-width: var(--col-body);
    }

    .markdown-body h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: var(--fs-display-md);
      line-height: var(--lh-display-md);
      letter-spacing: -0.012em;
      color: var(--ink);
      margin: var(--s-8) 0 var(--s-3);
      max-width: 32ch;
      padding-bottom: var(--s-3);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    }
    .markdown-body h2:first-child {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .markdown-body p {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-weight: 400;
      font-size: var(--fs-body-lg);
      line-height: var(--lh-body-lg);
      color: var(--ink);
      margin: 0 0 var(--s-5);
    }
    .markdown-body p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .markdown-body strong,
    .markdown-body b {
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .markdown-body em,
    .markdown-body i {
      font-style: normal;
      font-weight: 200;
    }

    .markdown-body a {
      color: var(--ink);
      text-decoration-color: var(--ink);
    }
    .markdown-body a:hover {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    }

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
     * /about/ photographic figure - the Sleeping Giant
     *
     * Visual register matches the chart canon: one hairline pure-
     * ink frame at the plot boundary; no drop shadow, no rounded
     * corners, no inner padding, no card pillow. The image sits
     * directly on paper, framed exactly the way a chart's plot
     * area is framed. Aspect is locked to 16:9 (the Tier-3 chart
     * aspect) so the figure feels native to the visual system.
     *
     * Caption sits below the frame, NOT inside it. Eyebrow uses
     * the same micro-caps treatment as the static page kicker
     * (Manrope 600, 10px, letter-spacing 0.22em, uppercase). The
     * credit line is the only italic in the static body and is
     * deliberately small - the eye reads the eyebrow first and
     * only needs the photographer attribution if it is hunting
     * for it. CC BY-SA 3.0 requires the credit; the visual hierarchy
     * respects the license without letting it dominate.
     * ---------------------------------------------------------- */

    .static__figure {
      margin: var(--s-7) 0 var(--s-7);
      padding: 0;
    }

    .static__figure-img {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center 40%;
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      border-radius: 0;
      box-shadow: none;
      background: var(--paper);
    }

    .static__figcaption {
      margin-top: 10px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .static__figcaption-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 10px;
      line-height: 1.4;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .static__figcaption-credit {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 400;
      font-size: 11px;
      line-height: 1.4;
      letter-spacing: 0;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
